{"title":"The housing winter arrives early as existing home sales crash to Great Recession levels and the long-feared ‘deep freeze’ sets in (Fortune, 2023-10-20T20:30:29+00:00)","text":"The housing winter arrives early as existing home sales crash to Great Recession levels and the long-feared ‘deep freeze’ sets in (Fortune, 2023-10-20T20:30:29+00:00)
Plus, the raising of interest rates in an effort to combat inflation is strikingly similar to the ’80s. Back then, Fed Chair Paul Volcker fought inflation through aggressive interest rate hikes, with the average 30-year fixed mortgage peaking at about 18% by late 1981. Sound familiar? Current Fed Chair Jerome Powell has set the tone for the most aggressive global hiking of rates in the modern era. And in due course, this week, mortgage rates hit 8%, the highest they’ve been in more than 20 years.

All things considered, home sales activity also plummeted from 1978 to 1982. Existing-home sales dropped 50% during that period, according to the Office of Policy Development and Research.","entities":["Paul Volcker","Fed","Fortune","interest rates","The housing winter arrives early as existing home sales crash to Great Recession levels and the long-feared ‘deep freeze’ sets in","Great Recession","Office of Policy Development and Research","Existing-home sales dropped 50%","30-year fixed mortgage peaked at about 18%","Mortgage rates hit 8%","mortgage rates","home sales","inflation","Jerome Powell"],"facts":["Buckle up for more ‘turbulence’ in the housing market, BofA says—it’s a housing recession, 1980s style -MENTIONS-> Paul Volcker","Buckle up for more ‘turbulence’ in the housing market, BofA says—it’s a housing recession, 1980s style -MENTIONS-> Fed","ASX to open lower; Wall Street falls as the clamp tightens from rising bond yields -MENTIONS-> Fed","ASX set to open lower as Wall Street closes September with more losses -MENTIONS-> Fed","ASX rises after Wall Street gains on rate optimism; Oil drops -MENTIONS-> Fed"]}

{"title":"Buckle up for more ‘turbulence’ in the housing market, BofA says—it’s a housing recession, 1980s style (Fortune, 2023-10-06T20:05:26+00:00)","text":"Buckle up for more ‘turbulence’ in the housing market, BofA says—it’s a housing recession, 1980s style (Fortune, 2023-10-06T20:05:26+00:00)
Park and her team noted that there are no “noticeable signs” of excess housing development today like there were back then, and households aren’t nearly as burdened by mortgage debt. Household mortgage debt represented roughly 65% of U.S. consumers’ disposable income in the second quarter, compared to 100% before the GFC. And the ratio of Americans’ mortgage debt to their real estate assets—also called loan-to-value—was just 27% in the second quarter, compared to over 40% in 2008 and roughly 50% in 2010, Bank of America’s data shows.

New legislation was also enacted since the GFC to help prevent worst-case scenarios in the housing market. One of the most obvious effects of these new laws is that there are far fewer risky adjustable-rate mortgages today.","entities":["Bank of America","Buckle up for more ‘turbulence’ in the housing market, BofA says—it’s a housing recession, 1980s style","excess housing development","mortgage debt","loan-to-value","adjustable-rate mortgages","new legislation","housing market","housing recession","Park","Fortune","GFC","U.S."],"facts":["Sen. Robert Menendez, facing bribery charges, stumps bank CEOs by asking how much their firms paid in settlements for allegedly ripping off consumers -MENTIONS-> Bank of America","Japan’s prime minister Kishida says: ‘reassess our economy’ -MENTIONS-> Bank of America","From a Turkey trot to a movie marathon, Friendsgiving celebrations that aren’t a sit-down dinner -MENTIONS-> Bank of America","Earnings week ahead: Amazon, Microsoft, Alphabet, Meta, Ford, GM and more -MENTIONS-> Bank of America","ASX to rise after interest rate hopes boost US shares -MENTIONS-> Bank of America"]}

{"title":"The housing winter arrives early as existing home sales crash to Great Recession levels and the long-feared ‘deep freeze’ sets in (Fortune, 2023-10-20T20:30:29+00:00)","text":"The housing winter arrives early as existing home sales crash to Great Recession levels and the long-feared ‘deep freeze’ sets in (Fortune, 2023-10-20T20:30:29+00:00)
After a long, hot summer that saw mortgage rates creep ever higher, October has brought an early winter for the housing market. Existing-home sales dropped a stunning 15% in September on a year-over-year basis to a seasonally adjusted annual rate of 3.96 million transactions, according to the National Association of Realtors (NAR). That’s the lowest figure in 13 years, since 2010, when the world economy, and particularly the U.S. housing market, were struggling to pull out of the Great Financial Crisis.

Contributing factors to the continuous decline in home transactions include surging mortgage rates (which just hit 8% this week—a record in the 21st century), low inventory levels, and home prices that refuse to stop rising. In other words, there aren’t enough homes to buy, money isn’t cheap anymore, and the ones for sale are too rich for most homebuyers’ blood.","entities":["housing market","Fortune","National Association of Realtors","Existing-home sales","Inventory levels","Homebuyers","Great Recession","Great Financial Crisis","The housing winter arrives early as existing home sales crash to Great Recession levels and the long-feared ‘deep freeze’ sets in","home prices","mortgage rates","U.S.","world economy"],"facts":["Buckle up for more ‘turbulence’ in the housing market, BofA says—it’s a housing recession, 1980s style -MENTIONS-> housing market","1980s Déjà Vu for the Housing Market -MENTIONS-> housing market","Bank of America -SAID-> housing market","Park -SAID-> housing market","Is Sam Bankman-Fried a bad ‘man’ or a good ‘boy’? Lawyers swap opening statements before first witnesses take the stand -PUBLISHED_BY-> Fortune"]}

